  "Specification": "BOSCO (Byzantine One-Step Consensus) protocol. Processes vote ECHO0 or ECHO1, then decide in one step if a supermajority threshold is met, or fall through to an underlying consensus. Models Byzantine faults via fixed faulty set. Specifies agreement lemmas and one-step decision properties.",
